{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider's exonerating route under POL-NS-04 fails at limb (a). The chat log carries exactly two messages and neither was sent by the rider: MSG-09104-001 is the SYSTEM 'Your driver has arrived' notice at 07:25:21 and MSG-09104-002 is the driver's own 'I have marked arrival.' at 07:25:40. There is no rider message giving her own position, naming an entrance, block, tower or bay, asking where the driver is, or saying she cannot see the vehicle - so the coordinating message limb (a) requires simply does not exist in this window.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-09104"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "payload.messages",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-04 limb (c) also fails, and on the rider's own device. The rider track runs from 07:25:30 to 07:30:50 and places her 519.46 m from the pickup pin, with rider_qualifying_fix_count of 0 against a rider presence radius of 100 m for the STANDARD zone class. The rider was not waiting at the pickup point either, so her account that the car 'never came to my block' is not corroborated by her own trace.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09104", "EV-TRIP-09104"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's record carries no anti-farming pattern on the two fields POL-NS-07 names and no others: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, short of the '4 or more' limb, and 1 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 120 is 0.008, short of the 0.08 limb. Because POL-NS-07 requires both limbs, its anti-farming branch does not trip on this driver, compensation is not withheld on that ground, and the escalation packet that branch prescribes - the one that directs the reviewer to refund the rider in full - is not engaged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-09104"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No abuse-based escalation trigger is available on the counters the policy actually reads. rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0, so neither limb (c) nor limb (d) of POL-NS-09 fires, and the lifetime counters (prior_no_show_flags, prior_disputes_filed) are context only under POL-GEN-01 and cannot be substituted for them. This case falls to be decided on this trip's own evidence, not on either party's history.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-09104", "EV-DPROF-09104"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The arrival event on this trip is not a bare, uncorroborated tap. The trip record records arrived_at 07:25:20 and a wait_time_min of 5.7 running to the 07:31:00 cancellation; the platform's own SYSTEM notification 'Your driver has arrived' went out at 07:25:21; the driver posted 'I have marked arrival.' at 07:25:40; and his statement on file is that he 'marked arrival and waited before cancelling'. The trace, for its part, places the driver 559.37 m from the pin across the same interval. The driver did not leave and return - there are no gaps, max_gap_sec is 0.0 and trace_distance_km is 0.0 - so this is not a driver who took another job and came back. If the Judge finds these admissible artifacts in direct conflict over arrival and dwell, POL-NS-09(b) applies: the open question of which measure governs is for a human reviewer, and the SGD 4.00 fee is held rather than refunded while that review is pending.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09104", "EV-GPS-09104", "EV-CHAT-09104"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.max_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(ii): record trip TRP-09104 as a false-arrival event against driver DRV-09104 — the trace contains no qualifying in-geofence GPS fix anywhere in the trip."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the SGD 4.00 no-show cancellation fee is refunded in full to the rider, and no driver compensation is payable. The disputed amount should not have been charged.\n\nThe charge fails the baseline test in POL-NS-01. The driver's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-09104, weight 1.0 — complete, 37 fixes at a 10 s cadence, no gaps, 100% coverage) places the vehicle 559.37 m from the Blk 180 Bukit Panjang Ring Rd pickup pin across the whole 07:25–07:31 interval, stationary. The driver never entered the 50 m arrival radius for a STANDARD pickup: derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count is 0, so POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails under POL-NS-02; and with no in-geofence fix the effective dwell is 0 s against the 300 s STANDARD minimum, so limb (c) fails too. Because POL-NS-01 is conjunctive, the fee is not chargeable. The trip record's 'arrived' tap at 07:25:20 and its wait_time_min of 5.7 do not help: POL-NS-01(c) and POL-NS-05 provide that the waiting clock runs from GPS entry into the geofence, not from the marker.\n\nPOL-NS-05 is engaged. The 07:25:20 arrival marker was set while the driver was 559.37 m from the pin, past the 300 m threshold, so it is a false marker and does not start the clock. Recomputing from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, there is none anywhere in the trip, so POL-NS-05(ii) applies squarely: the fee is refunded in full, no compensation is payable, and the trip is recorded as a false-arrival event against the driver (the referral above). POL-NS-06 states the same arithmetic — a 300 s shortfall on a 300 s minimum refunds the fee — and limb (i) cannot rescue it: the only traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-09104-01) is MISSING at weight 0.0, there is no qualifying KERB_RESTRICTION/ENFORCEMENT/CLOSURE/ACCIDENT, and there are no separate in-geofence intervals to accumulate.\n\nThe driver's argument that this should escalate under POL-NS-09(b) is rejected. There is no unresolved conflict between admissible artifacts: the 'arrived' tap and wait_time record only that the driver set the marker, and POL-NS-01(c) and POL-NS-05 expressly resolve how that marker is read against the trace. The other escalation triggers do not fire either — the deciding facts rest on weight-1.0 artifacts, so there is no POL-NS-08(a)–(d) impairment and no POL-NS-09(e); both profiles show 0 disputes with each other in the trailing 90 days (no POL-NS-09(c)); the anti-farming check does not trip, since no_show_terminations_30d is 1 (below 4) and 1/120 = 0.008 (below 0.08); and rider no_show_disputes_30d is 0 (no POL-NS-09(d)).\n\nOn the remaining points: the rider is not exonerated under POL-NS-04 (no coordinating rider message appears in the chat log, and her own device sat about 519 m from the pin), but that does not assist the driver, because the refund follows from the GPS evidence under POL-NS-02, POL-NS-05 and POL-NS-06 regardless. POL-NS-03 does not engage — it reaches only a driver stationary within 400 m of the pin, and the closest approach was 559.37 m — so there is no wrong-entrance finding and no pin-ambiguity goodwill payment. No driver compensation is payable: POL-NS-07 is not satisfied, and POL-NS-05(ii) says so in terms. On the money, the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-09104, weight 1.0) shows a SGD 4.00 cancellation fee charged against a SGD 0.00 base fare on a trip that never started; SGD 4.00 is returned."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "POL-NS-06 states the arithmetic directly: an effective in-geofence dwell of 0 seconds against the 300 second STANDARD minimum is a 300 second shortfall, and on that shortfall the cancellation fee is refunded to the rider in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded to messages. The driver cannot rescue the computation under POL-NS-06(i), because there are no separate in-geofence intervals to accumulate and no traffic advisory on file.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason": "Cites EV-ADVIS-09104-01, whose weight_multiplier is 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, without disclosing that impairment or naming the issue code, as Step 1(c)/POL-GEN-02(1) requires. The claim uses the advisory's absence but says nothing about the artifact's weight or the codes that fired. (The underlying shortfall point survives via the POL-NS-01, POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-05 claims.)"
    }
  ]
}
